  "job_B1.5.7_20251001_193248": {
    "text": "Simile est regnum celorum homini regi & religua.\nCristes iwun\u00e6 w\u00e6s \u00f0\u00e6t he wolde oft sp\u00e6c\u00e6n on deopum bigspellum to his discipulis; \u00f0a s\u00e6de he hwilon\nHeofene rice is ilic ane kynge, he \u00f0e h\u00e6fde mot wi\u00f0 his men hwilon & wolde mid gesceade settan his\nHe sp\u00e6c \u00fea wi\u00f0 \u00e6nne mon \u00fee him ahte to geldene ten \u00feusend pund\u00e6, & manode him \u00fe\u00e6s feos.\n\u00d0a n\u00e6fde \u00fee \u00f0egen nane mihte to \u00feam \u00fe\u00e6t he \u00f0am laforde his lane forgylde; ac \u00fee laford het \u00fea l\u00e6don\n\u00dea feol \u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6gen adun to his lafordes fotum & b\u00e6d hine georne mid \u00feissum worde, cw\u00e6\u00f0ende, La,\n\u00d0e laford \u00fea mildsode \u00feam \u00f0egene \u00feerrihte, & l\u00e6t hine faren, & all \u00fe\u00e6t feoh him forgeaf.\n\u00d0a eode \u00fee \u00f0egen ut; & he efne \u00fea imette sumne o\u00f0erne mon of his agenum iferum, \u00fee ahte him to\n& il\u00e6hte hine son\u00e6, & l\u00e6gde hine adun & hine of\u00f0ryhte, \u00f0us cw\u00e6\u00f0ende him to, Ageld nu swi\u00f0e ra\u00f0\u00e6\n\u00d0a ge\u00e6lnode \u00f0e o\u00f0er hine up swa \u00f0eah, & feol to his fotum fyrstes him biddende.\nBihet \u00fe\u00e6t he wolde al his feoh him forgeld\u00e6n.\n\u00dea nolde \u00fee \u00f0egen l\u00e6ten him n\u00e6nne fyrst, ac sette hine on cwearterne mid swi\u00f0licum gram\u00e6 o\u00f0 \u00f0et he\n\u00d0a is\u00e6gen \u00fea hiredmen hu \u00f0e \u00feegen dyde embe \u00f0one o\u00f0erne, & unrodsoden unglededon swi\u00f0e &\n\u00d0e kyng het \u00fea son\u00e6 hine clypi\u00e6n him to, & cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00f0us mid yrre, Eal\u00e6, \u00f0u, yfel\u00e6 \u00f0eow\u00e6, ic forgeaf \u00fee\n\u00d0a yrsode \u00f0e laford, ant l\u00e6t hine bit\u00e6cen \u00feam sti\u00f0um witnerum, \u00fee hine witni\u00e6n sceolden, o\u00f0 \u00f0et he\nNu s\u00e6g\u00f0 us \u00feis godspel \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fee H\u00e6lend \u00fea s\u00e6de.\nAl swa de\u00fe to so\u00f0an min heofenlice F\u00e6der eow, gif ge ne forgif\u00e6\u00f0 eowrum gebro\u00f0rum, \u00e6lc an of his\nHer is mucel andgit eow monnum to witenne; & we nim\u00e6\u00f0 her to to \u00f0issere trahtnunge Augustinum\nHeofene rice is ihaten on \u00f0issere stowe Godes agene la\u00f0ung, \u00fe\u00e6t is, al Godes folc, \u00f0e rihtlice ilef\u00e6\u00f0 on\n\u00d0e H\u00e6lend cw\u00e6\u00f0 hwilon to \u00feam halgan Petrum \u00f0us, Gif \u00fein bro\u00f0or syneg\u00e6\u00f0 wi\u00f0 \u00fee, cy\u00f0 him\nGif he \u00fee ihyr\u00e6\u00f0, swa \u00f0u strynest hine Gode.\nGif he \u00fee ne ihyr\u00e6\u00f0, hafe \u00f0e to gewit\u00e6n \u00e6nne bro\u00f0or o\u00f0\u00f0e twegen, & \u00f0rea hine eft swa; ant gif he him\nGif he \u00f0onne ne gehyr\u00f0 \u00f0a halga la\u00f0unge, beo he \u00f0enne \u00e6lfremed, swa swa h\u00e6\u00f0en mon from \u00f0e.\n\u00d0a axode Petrus, Hu ofte sceal ic forgif\u00e6n?\nBi\u00f0 inoh seofen si\u00f0um?\n& him s\u00e6de \u00f0e H\u00e6lend, Ne s\u00e6cge ic na seofen si\u00f0um; ac \u00f0u scealt forgifan seofon si\u00f0on gewis, &\n\u00d0a s\u00e6de him \u00f0e H\u00e6lend sy\u00f0\u00f0an \u00feis bigspel, swa swa we hwene \u00e6r eow s\u00e6den on Englisc.\nFor \u00fean \u00f0e he us l\u00e6rde mid \u00feare licness, & nolde \u00fe\u00e6t we loseden, from his lufe \u00e6lfr\u00e6mede.\n\u00c6lc mon eornestlice ah to geldene sum \u00feing, ant h\u00e6f\u00f0 o\u00f0erne mon \u00fee him sceal sum \u00f0ing; for\u00feon \u00f0e\nNu sette God sylf us \u00feesne regol betwyx us, \u00fe\u00e6t we \u00feam forgifan \u00fee wi\u00f0 us agylt\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t God us forgife\nTwa weorc beo\u00f0 \u00feare so\u00f0an mildsunge \u00fee us alys\u00e6\u00f0 be Cristes sylfes lare.\nDimitte & dimittetur uobis, date & dabitur uobis, He cw\u00e6\u00f0, Forgife ge, and eow bi\u00f0 forgifen.\nDo\u00f0 god o\u00f0rum monnum, & eow bi\u00f0 god igifen.\n\u00d0u bist mildsunge \u00e6t Gode; milds\u00e6 \u00f0u o\u00f0re men.\n\u00d0u wylt underfon god; ty\u00f0\u00e6 \u00f0u o\u00f0re men, na for \u00f0issum life ane, ac for \u00feam ece life, \u00f0\u00e6r \u00f0e bi\u00f0\nNu mage we axi\u00e6n swa swa Petrus axode, Hu ofte we sceolon o\u00f0rum monnum forgif\u00e6n?\n\u00c6lce d\u00e6ge we bidd\u00e6\u00fe ure synne forgifennysse on \u00feam paternoster, swa swa Crist sylf us gesette \u00fe\u00e6t\nNu acso\u00f0 God \u00fee hu fel\u00e6 synna he forgife \u00fee, \u00feenne s\u00e6gest \u00f0u, alle; do \u00feu al swa \u00f0e sylf forgif allum\nHw\u00e6t gem\u00e6n\u00f0 \u00feonne ic cw\u00e6\u00f0e \u00fe\u00e6t monigfealde getel seofen & hundseofentig?\nNu s\u00e6g\u00f0 us Augustinus mycele tacnunge be \u00f0am get\u00e6le \u00feus.\n\u00d0a \u00fea ure H\u00e6lend w\u00e6s her on life ifullod, \u00fea tealde \u00fee godspellere Lucas from Criste sylfum upweard\nAnt Matheus \u00fee godspellere ongon to tellenne fram Abrahame duneweard o\u00f0\u00f0et Cristes acennednysse.\nHe tealde ni\u00f0erweard hu Crist com to middanearde, & Lucas tealde upweard fram Cristes fulluhte,\nOn his fulluhte w\u00e6ron heofen\u00e6s iopenode, \u00f0\u00e6t iseah Iohannes, \u00fee hine fullode, & Lucas tealde \u00feanon,\nNu n\u00e6s nan m\u00e6g\u00f0 forl\u00e6ten \u00e6fre from men to o\u00f0rum; ne nan synna \u00fe\u00e6t ne sceal beon forgifen.\nFor\u00fean \u00f0e on \u00f0am fulluhte beo\u00f0 alle synna forgifen\u00e6, \u00f0anon \u00fee Lucas tealde \u00fea m\u00e6gracan upweard.\n\u00d0a \u00f0a \u00f0e H\u00e6lend wolde her on life beon acenned on \u00feare seofan m\u00e6g\u00f0e & \u00f0are hundseofenteo\u00f0an\nGit \u00fe\u00e6r is o\u00f0er tacnuncg alswa deop swa \u00f0is.\nGodes lage w\u00e6s isett \u00feurh hine sylfne, iwriten on twam st\u00e6nene weaxbr\u00e6den mid tyn ealicum wordum,\nNu is \u00fe\u00e6t tynfealde getel on \u00f0am tyn \u00f0usend\u00e6, swa fela \u00f0usend pund\u00e6 sceolde \u00fee \u00f0\u00e6gen \u00feam kynge; &\nOn \u00f0am tenfealde get\u00e6le bi\u00f0 Godes lage ifylled; & on endlyf\u00e6nfealde bi\u00f0 \u00feeo forgeagednysse \u00fe\u00e6t mon\nFor\u00feyg weron itealde on \u00feam Godes it\u00e6lde, \u00fee Moyses wrohte on \u00feam w\u00e6stene, \u00fea alles endlyf\u00e6n\n\u00dea endlyf\u00e6n w\u00e6ron h\u00e6rene for \u00f0are d\u00e6\u00febote and for \u00feare andetnysse mid bireowsunge, \u00fee \u00f0e mon\nNu forgeaf \u00fee kyng, swa swa \u00f0is godspel cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00e6r, alne \u00feone mycele gylt mildelice \u00feam \u00feegene, \u00f0eah\nHe nolde gety\u00f0ian \u00f0\u00e6t \u00f0\u00e6t him w\u00e6s ity\u00f0od, & he wear\u00f0 \u00fea bit\u00e6ht to tintregienne \u00feam sti\u00f0um\nNu s\u00e6g\u00f0 us \u00feis godspel \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fee H\u00e6lend \u00fea s\u00e6de, All swa de\u00fe to so\u00f0an min heofenlice F\u00e6der eow, gif\nJohannes \u00fee apostol, \u00f0e w\u00e6s eac godsp\u00e6llere, awrat on his pistole \u00f0issum wordum cw\u00e6\u00f0ende, Si\nGif we \u00f0onne andette\u00f0 ure synn\u00e6n geornlice, God bi\u00f0 us itreowe, & eac swi\u00f0e rihtwis, & forgyf\u00e6\u00f0 us\nWe sceolon forgyf\u00e6n \u00f0am \u00f0e wi\u00f0 us agylt\u00e6\u00f0, swa swa \u00f0e H\u00e6lend s\u00e6de, be \u00f0am \u00f0e ge sylfe herdon, of\nAc ne cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00feu na mid wordum \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu wylle mildsi\u00e6n, & \u00e6lcige swa\u00f0eah wi\u00f0inn\u00e6n \u00f0inre heortan;\nGod cw\u00e6\u00f0 eft nu to \u00fee, Ic forgife nu \u00e6rest \u00fee; forgif \u00feu hure sy\u00f0\u00f0an; & gif \u00f0u swa ne dest on eornost,\nAc Augustinus us s\u00e6g\u00f0 \u00f0\u00e6t mon steor\u00e6n sceal his agene childum mid \u00e6ge & mid lufe, hwilon mid\n\u00d0\u00e6t bi\u00f0 yfel ge\u00f0yld \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u i\u00f0afige \u00feinum bearne \u00fe\u00e6t he on fr\u00e6cednesse fare mid his dysige, and \u00feu\n\u00d0am stuntum monne mon sceal steor\u00e6n \u00e6fre but\u00e6n \u00e6lcere hatunge, & hine rihtl\u00e6cen; \u00f0a \u00f0e styr\u00e6n\nAll swa \u00f0e l\u00e6ce de\u00fe \u00f0e l\u00e6cn\u00e6\u00f0 \u00feene mon, \u00fee pin\u00e6\u00f0 on \u00f0a wund\u00e6 \u00f0\u00e6t heo wur\u00f0\u00e6 ih\u00e6led.\nFor\u00fean \u00f0e \u00f0e mon los\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fee lige\u00f0 yfele forwundod, gif \u00fee l\u00e6ce him ar\u00e6\u00f0 & nyle mid sti\u00f0nesse \u00fea\nNu beo\u00f0 sume gult\u00e6s, swa swa us s\u00e6cg\u00e6\u00f0 bec, \u00f0e mon digollice sceal mid gesceade betan, & sume\nGif \u00f0e gylt beo digle, bet \u00feu hine digollice, and ne m\u00e6lde \u00feu nateshwon hine o\u00f0rum monnum; and gif\n\u00d0u \u00fee styran scealt, \u00fe\u00e6t he seolf beo irihtl\u00e6ht, & o\u00f0re beon istyrede, \u00f0e \u00fea steor ihyr\u00e6\u00f0.\n\u00deus t\u00e6c\u00e6\u00f0 us \u00fe\u00e6t godspel and \u00fee Godes apostol.\n\u00d0e \u00f0e monhat\u00e6 bi\u00f0, ne m\u00e6g he w\u00e6l styr\u00e6n; for\u00fean \u00f0e \u00fea halga wer\u00e6s \u00f0e weron iu lareow\u00e6s beo\u00f0 nu\nBeo him a a wur\u00f0mynt and wuldor, Amen, Amen.",
